  "prompt_text": "The figure summarizes beneficial systemic effects across several organs and cell types, using simple icons and short text. Overall, it highlights a treatment or mechanism that reduces inflammatory damage while strengthening vascular and tissue barriers.\n\nIn the brain, the main message is improved blood–brain barrier function, with less leakage and a reduced interferon-related inflammatory signature. It also appears to help correct an imbalance between regulatory T cells and T helper 17 cells. In the kidney, similar protective effects are emphasized: reduced IgG deposition, proteinuria, and immune-complex deposition, alongside better endothelial barrier function, less leukocyte passage into tissue, and a lower interferon signature. The same Treg–Th17 balance is noted there as well.\n\nA blood vessel panel suggests cardiovascular protection, showing decreased atherosclerotic injury, stronger endothelial barrier integrity, and reduced expression of pro-inflammatory adhesion molecules. Finally, an immune-cell panel indicates reduced type I interferon production by plasmacytoid dendritic cells.\n\nTaken together, the image presents a coordinated anti-inflammatory and barrier-protective model affecting the central nervous system, kidneys, vasculature, and innate immune signaling.",
